[issue.1680]
number = 1680
title = "[Coherence] The legacy REST body limit is a fixed 1,000,000-byte constant, while the API server's limit comes from the operator's rpc-max-body-bytes setting"
revision = "bb8caac8b3e73e3e2f4b330805574f0bcb540641"
verdict = "task"
evidence = "The cap introduced by commit a2a291cb095768b9204db48886ccffe6a65f5d79 remains at sdk/types/rest/rest.go:29 and sdk/types/rest/rest.go:151, and its 413 message at sdk/types/rest/rest.go:155 ignores the matched MaxBytesError limit even though sdk/server/api/server.go:108 supplies RPCMaxBodyBytes (default 1000000 at sdk/server/config/config.go:279) to the outer reader at consensus/rpc/jsonrpc/server/http_server.go:64 and consensus/rpc/jsonrpc/server/http_server.go:259, while sdk/types/rest/repair_m650_test.go:187 tests only the default cap."
close_comment = "The mismatch is confirmed and tracked by task 18.1680.1 to report the byte limit that actually rejected a legacy REST request. The correction retains the 1,000,000-byte REST cap and reports a smaller configured API limit when that limit is exceeded."

